  "facts": [
    "Opened May 10, 1973, the General Manuel Belgrano Bridge spans 1,700 meters, rising 35 meters above the Paraná River, and features a dramatic cable‑stayed section with 245‑meter central span flanked by 163.5‑meter arms.",
    "Its two A‑shaped towers soar 83 meters, anchoring the cable‑stayed spans that carry an 8.3‑meter wide road with two lanes, plus pedestrian walkways each 1.8 meters wide.",
    "In December 1999, the bridge became a flashpoint when demonstrators blocked traffic, prompting a gendarmerie crackdown that tragically killed two protestors, a case still under investigation."
